      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What you are describing sounds like a deep, overwhelming grief or hopelessness that is feeling completely isolating and exhausting. When pain is this all-consuming, the mind can sometimes mistake giving up for the only outcome that would bring relief, but please know that your situation does not have to end this way. There are specialized, compassionate resources that specifically understand this feeling of being trapped where standard advice often falls short. Reaching out to a grief specialist, a crisis counselor, or a trusted local support group might offer a different kind of witness than the usual medical or financial advice.",
      "source": "target",
